          <input type="number" step="0.01" name="collexia_max_single_mandate_amount" class="form-control" value="<?= e($settings['collexia_max_single_mandate_amount'] ?? '') ?>" placeholder="Blank = no local limit enforced">
          <div class="form-text">
            Collexia rejects a mandate above some amount with "10569 Mandate amount limit exceeded" --
            confirmed by evidence (N$548.33 registered fine; N$1,096.66 was rejected). Collexia has since
            confirmed (2026-09-15) this limit only exists in the sandbox/UAT environment and will not apply
            once live in production. This is a locally-configured safety limit, checked before DesertLedger
            even attempts a placement -- <strong>blank this field before going live</strong> so production
            placements are never blocked by a UAT-only restriction. The related per-installment limit
            ("10570 Installment amount limit exceeded") is confirmed UAT-only too -- see Known System
            Behaviors below.
